message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below, together with the book whose frameworks it develops."
title: "FCRL-energy: fair and sustainable allocation of energy support under price shocks"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-07"
authors:
  - family-names: Sargiotis
    given-names: Dimitrios
    affiliation: "School of Civil Engineering, National Technical University of Athens"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-3644-4561"
repository-code: "https://github.com/uomoathens/fcrl-energy"
abstract: >-
  Runnable, tested decision system developed from the FCRL-MARL, SC-RL and
  XRL-URM frameworks of AI with Integrity (Springer, 2026). It shares a fixed
  energy support budget among regions before need is known, guarantees every
  region a minimum share of its need through adaptive conformal inference that
  stays valid after price shocks, shares the rest with a policy trained to
  protect the worst-off regions first while avoiding support above need, and
  explains every allocation in plain language. It is evaluated on synthetic
  data and on Eurostat degree-day, poverty, population and energy price data
  for the NUTS 2 regions of Greece, Bulgaria, Spain, Portugal and Italy, with
  stress tests for price rises and budget cuts.
keywords:
  - energy poverty
  - energy support
  - fair allocation
  - multi-agent reinforcement learning
  - conformal prediction
  - prioritarian welfare
  - explainable AI
  - sustainability
  - Eurostat
